            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "There are more inventory related events in dbus-sensors.\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/dbus-sensors/blob/master/src/fan/PresenceGpio.hpp#L30\n\nBut I am hunting down what `deviceType` options there are."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "1.0.0, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Trying to ensure this generates OpenBMC.0.1.InventoryAdded as https://github.com/openbmc/entity-manager/blob/master/src/entity_manager.hpp#L149C22-L149C48."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "The design for events said we were going to deprecate the old events.  We shouldn't try to map to any of the old \"OpenBMC.*\" ones."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This will create \"OpenBMC_InventoryInventory.0.0.InventoryRemoved\" as you currently have it specified.  You might want to move the Inventory.events up a level?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for catching that. I moved it out."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Why is \"InventoryRemoved\" a warning?  Hardware can often be plugged and unplugged while a BMC is in some state of running, depending on the system design.  I don't think this should be an error.\n\nIf we have an error because a _Required_ piece of hardware has been removed, we need to be more explicit on the error defined here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Yeah, EM always had this as an event. I can bump down the priority of this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Technically, EM has both these as events. But I think removed can use a little bump in priority."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 5,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "It is concerning to me that we'd be exposing an entity-manager \"Type\" string that doesn't necessarily correlate to anything documented or anything elsewhere in the system.  How would a daemon like PLDM properly fill one of these in?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 14,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Removed all of those and used an object_path instead. That would be more usable across all other inventory types."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How do we decide that these are the set required?  Model vs PN vs SparePart Number... I bet people have differing opinions here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Removed these in favor of object_path."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 28,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "There is no resolution?  \ud83d\ude04  Wouldn't it be plug it back in?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Inventory.events.yaml",
                    "line": 28,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
